// Every row of the runtime's `f64` math table (`runtime/src/math/bits.rs`) through compiled code,
// one result per line, then `sin`, `cos`, `atan2`, `exp`, `log` and `pow` of six `float` inputs,
// then every row of the `float` table (`runtime/src/math/bits_float.rs`). `f64` math is the
// runtime's `libm` functions; `float` math is computed in `float` by the wide functions, never
// widened to `f64`. Printing is the shortest text that reads back as the same value, so equal text
// is equal bits (NaN aside). `print_table` in `bits.rs` and `print_float_table` in `bits_float.rs`
// print these lines. Kestrel has no exponent in literals: the long literals are 1e300, 1e22,
// 1e-300, 1e-310 and the smallest subnormal, 5e-324 for `f64`, and 1e30, 3.4028235e38, 1e-40, 3e-41
// and 1e-45 for `float`.
